" Title: Meridian Marine Ltd Travel and Expense Claims Policy\n\n1. Introduction\nMeridian Marine Ltd is committed to ensuring fair and consistent practices for travel and expense claims. This policy outlines the guidelines for employees who are required to travel on company business, detailing the approved methods of claiming expenses incurred during such travels.\n\n2. Daily Meal Allowance\nEmployees will receive a daily meal allowance of USD 50 while on business trips, with exceptions made for locations where costs are significantly higher or lower. The per diem rates for different locations can be found in the Expense Policy Manual available on our internal portal.\n\n3. Accommodation\n- Hotel nightly cap: Employees are limited to a USD 150 nightly cap for hotel accommodation, with exceptions made for high-cost cities or when justified by business needs.\n- Shared rooms: When traveling with colleagues, employees are encouraged to share rooms to minimize costs. Exceptions may be granted upon request and approval from the Travel Manager.\n\n4. Transportation\nFlight booking classes will depend on travel duration as follows:\n- Domestic flights (< 3 hours): Economy class\n- International short-haul flights (3 \u2013 6 hours): Premium economy class\n- International long-haul flights (> 6 hours): Business class\n\n5. Ground Transportation\nReasonable costs associated with ground transportation, such as taxis, public transport, or rental cars, will be reimbursed. Employees are encouraged to use cost-effective options whenever possible.\n\n6. Mileage Rate\nFor personal vehicle usage during business trips, a mileage rate of USD 0.54 per kilometer (round trip) will be applied.\n\n7. Incidentals and Receipts\nReceipts are mandatory for expenses exceeding USD 100. Incidental expenses (e.g., phone calls, internet usage, laundry services) should be reasonable and necessary for the successful completion of company business.\n\n8. Submission Deadline\nEmployees must submit travel claims within 30 days following their return to ensure timely processing and reimbursement. Late claims may be subject to approval from the Travel Manager or Finance Department.\n\n9. Approval Thresholds and Authorization\n- Claims up to USD 500 can be approved by a Team Leader or direct supervisor.\n- Claims between USD 501 and USD 2,000 require approval from the Travel Manager.\n- Claims exceeding USD 2,000 must be reviewed and approved by both the Travel Manager and a member of the Finance Department (e.g., Financial Controller or Director of Finance).\n\n10. Compliance and Monitoring\nNoncompliance with this policy may result in denied claims or disciplinary actions as outlined in our Employee Handbook. Regular audits will be conducted to ensure adherence to these guidelines. Any questions regarding this policy should be directed to the Travel Manager or HR department."